          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Make the best five-card poker hand using Deuces as wild cards. In Diablo mode, the opener must win the pot or match it to fund the next hand.',
          gameplay: "1. Ante: Standard ante from all players.\n2. Deal: 5 cards to each player.\n3. First Betting Round: Standard poker betting begun by player to dealer's left.\n4. The Draw: Active players may discard and draw a MAXIMUM of two cards.\n5. Second Betting Round: Standard betting begun by the player who opened the first round.\n6. Showdown: Best hand wins the pot.\n7. Diablo rule: If the opener does not win, the opener contributes an amount equal to the just-won pot to seed the next hand. Deal passes left and the next hand is played with no new antes. The cycle continues until a hand in which the opener wins.",
          keyRules: [
            'Deuces (2s) are wild.',
            'Max draw of 2 cards.',
            'Openers must win or match the pot.',
            'Standard poker hand rankings with Five of a Kind as highest hand.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Be extremely cautious about opening the pot. If your hand is marginal, checking is safer to avoid the 'Match the Pot' penalty.",
          intermediate: "Since everyone knows Deuces are wild, 'Trips' are the new 'Pair.' Don't bother staying in the hand without at least a natural pair or a wild card.",
          advanced: "Positional opening: If you are the dealer and it's checked to you, opening is less risky because you have seen everyone else's lack of interest. However, if you open and lose, you pay. Use the threat of the 'Match' to force folds if you have a strong hand.",
          tips: [
            "Don't open on a bluff unless you have the chips to cover a pot-match.",
            'If you hold two deuces, you have a powerhouse - opening is usually correct.',
            "Track the 'Diablo' pot size; it can grow very fast.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
